@startuml state_machines_http_parser
!theme cyborg
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam state {
 BackgroundColor #16324a
 BorderColor #4aa3df
 FontColor #e6edf7
 BackgroundColor<<terminal>> #3a1d22
 BorderColor<<terminal>> #e06c75
 BackgroundColor<<finding>> #3a2a12
 BorderColor<<finding>> #e5a50a
 BackgroundColor<<documented>> #273241
 BorderColor<<documented>> #61738a
 FontColor<<documented>> #b8c4d4
}
skinparam note {
 BackgroundColor #1b2330
 BorderColor #61738a
 FontColor #e6edf7
}
hide empty description
title HTTP response reader: which parser events end one response?\n(implemented; wifi_http.c, one wifi_http_reader per exchange, Zephyr http_parser callbacks)
state "Status line" as Status
state "Header name\nheaderNameLength" as HeaderName
state "Header value\nisInHeaderValue, isReadingLocation" as HeaderValue
state "Body\nbodyLength; drains on overflow\n(bodyHasOverflowed)" as Body
state "Complete\nisComplete; parser paused;\nkeepsConnection = keep-alive ∧ no overflow\n∧ no bytes behind the message" as Complete <<terminal>>
state "Failed\nfailure (first error wins)" as Failed <<terminal>>
state "Interim 1xx taken as final\n(H1, reproduced on host)" as Interim <<finding>>
[*] --> Status
Status --> HeaderName : on_status
HeaderName --> HeaderValue : on_header_value
HeaderValue --> HeaderName : on_header_field\n(next header)
HeaderValue --> Body : on_headers_complete
HeaderName --> Body : on_headers_complete
Body --> Complete : on_message_complete, or close-delimited end\n(wifi_finishHttpResponse)
HeaderValue --> Interim : status 100 to 199 ends without body:\non_message_complete
Interim --> Complete : status = 1xx;\nthe final response stays unread
Status --> Failed : parser error, header or Location limit
HeaderName --> Failed
HeaderValue --> Failed
Body --> Failed
note bottom of Interim
 Missing transition. A possible fix (not decided): for 1xx other than 101, reset and parse the next message.
 If the final response arrives in a later TLS record, the connection is kept with it unread,
 and the next exchange reads it as its own response. Triggered only by a server or proxy
 (103 Early Hints, unsolicited 100 Continue); the device sends no Expect header.
end note
note right of Complete
 Any further read returns -EBADMSG.
end note
@enduml
